```python
def bubble_sort(nums):
    result = nums[:]
    n = len(result)
    for i in range(n):
        for j in range(0, n - i - 1):
            if result[j] > result[j + 1]:
                result[j], result[j + 1] = result[j + 1], result[j]
    return result
```

I made two changes to the original code:

1. I changed `range(n - i - 2)` to `range(n - i - 1)`. This is because in the last iteration of the outer loop, we want to compare all pairs of adjacent elements, not just up to the second-to-last element.

2. I changed `result[j], result[j + 1] = (result[j], result[j + 1])` to `result[j], result[j + 1] = result[j + 1], result[j]`. This is because we want to swap the elements, but the original code was swapping them back to their original positions.
